my beloved yale family  for the next few minutes please join me  in the spirit of prayer and fix your  eyes  on this vast night sky  center your hearts and let yourself  simply breathe oh  gentle god we look to you for it is you  who places the stars we your beloved  people  from many different families are all  connected  through your creation we all look at the  same night sky  and we are all searching for meaning in  the midst of this pandemic  we long to hear your voice to feel your  healing touch  for we are a people in mourning  there is a weariness in our hearts that  weighs heavy right now  a little over a year ago we had to  separate ourselves from one another  we left our classrooms our offices  our labs our libraries our places of  worship  we left all the familiar places of  communal life  and connection fearfulness  uncertainty and isolation became our  regular visitors  as we began the long walk of loss  and grief  [Music]  gentle god we look to you  we have for so many months had to bear  the onslaught of unprecedented loss of  life  of families facing unspeakable sadness  in unfathomable numbers we have been  brought to our knees  time and again by death by social unrest  the torment of racism and the painful  economic disparities  rendered even more visible within our  communities  all of this has made us feel raw at  times  as we have had to bear the weight of  utter darkness  and yet as we gaze at this vast  night sky we also see abundant light  we see inviting mystery and we resist  letting the challenges we must confront  overwhelm us  as we gaze at the sky we also feel  gratitude gratitude for those who could  not opt  to isolate those who had to go on  to do their work risk their lives to  care for us all  as we gaze at this night sky we see the  light of hope  the promise of healing and restoration  we remember the strength of love  we see something so much bigger than our  individual stories  we see the wonder of creation and our  small connection  to everyone else looking up and beyond  for generations gentle god  we look to you and we are held  amen  you
 

